Changes for ioBroker: src-www/src is the upstream source with only its names changed; tasks.ts patches it at build
time (ioBroker theme, local help links, texts, own styles and furniture), and the code added to it is in
frontend/vendor-ext/. The page around it (frontend/) connects it to ioBroker over the socket of the web adapter.
Not an official Mastershort release. Furniture packs and add-ons sold in the upstream shop are not included; the
modules for pools and devices are written for ioBroker.

Bundled third-party libraries: three.js with its loaders (MIT, www/licenses/three-MIT.txt), the meshoptimizer
decoder that comes with three.js (MIT, www/licenses/meshoptimizer-MIT.txt), Lit (BSD-3-Clause,
www/licenses/lit-BSD.txt), icons of @mdi/js (Apache-2.0, www/licenses/mdi-Apache-2.0.txt), fonts Figtree and
Bricolage Grotesque (OFL, www/vendor/fonts/). The dialogs of the page bundle React, MUI, Emotion,
@iobroker/gui-components and @iobroker/socket-client (MIT and others): the build lists every package bundled into
the page with its license in www/licenses/page-licenses.md.
